        "## 3. Methodology\n",
        "\n",
        "### Task type\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scoring / ranking built on binary classification.** Logistic Regression outputs a probability of the proxy decline label; that probability becomes the ranking score.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Target\n",
        "\n",
        "`is_declining_label = (trend_direction == \"down\")`\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a **proxy for current observed decline**, not a future outcome. W02 explicitly identifies the stronger warehouse design as prior-window features predicting a later-window decline.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Primary metric\n",
        "\n",
        "**Precision@50** — because the actual workflow starts at the top of a human review queue.\n",
        "\n",
        "Supporting metrics such as ROC-AUC and average precision can be inspected, but they are not the main decision metric.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Baseline\n",
        "\n",
        "The W04 transparent rule is re-scored on the **same held-out client split**:\n",
        "\n",
        "`visible × (1 + stale_flag + ctr_weak_flag) × log1p(impressions_90d)`\n",
        "\n",
        "where:\n",
        "\n",
        "- visible = `impressions_90d >= 250`\n",
        "- stale = `days_since_last_update >= 90`\n",
        "- CTR weak = visible page with `1 <= avg_position <= 20` and `ctr < 0.30`\n",
        "\n",
        "### Model\n",
        "\n",
        "The final W05/W07 Logistic Regression uses:\n",
        "\n",
        "- numeric search/content/engagement signals\n",
        "- missingness indicators\n",
        "- log-transformed impressions, clicks, sessions\n",
        "- categorical content/intent/competition/age/freshness features\n",
        "- standardized numeric features + one-hot categorical features\n",
        "\n",
        "`Random Forest` is retained as a comparison model, not as the deployed choice.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Validation split\n",
        "\n",
        "**GroupShuffleSplit, 80/20, seed 42, grouped by `client_id`.**\n",
        "\n",
        "This prevents the same client's pages appearing in both train and test.\n"
      ]
    },
