      "source": [
        "### Model interpretation and error review\n",
        "\n",
        "The chosen model is Logistic Regression because it is simpler and materially stronger than Random Forest on the same split. The coefficients provide directional clues, but they are **not causal explanations**.\n",
        "\n",
        "W05's manual error review found a useful boundary case: two false positives had very similar low-click/low-engagement profiles, while a false negative was an unranked page (`avg_position == 0`). This motivated W07's separate **technical-check lane** for unranked pages rather than trusting the model probability alone.\n"
      ]
    },
