        "## 8. Five-Minute Demo Outline\n",
        "\n",
        "**0:00–0:45 — Question.** FlyRank's editors can review roughly 20–50 pages a week, while the catalog is about 30,000 pages. Which pages should be opened first?\n",
        "\n",
        "**0:45–2:00 — Method.** Transparent rule baseline vs. client-grouped Logistic Regression, evaluated on the identical held-out split. Explain the label-proxy limitation and the leakage audit.\n",
        "\n",
        "**2:00–3:00 — Result.** Show Precision@50: **0.34 baseline → 0.86 Logistic Regression**; Random Forest reaches **0.52** on the same split.\n",
        "\n",
        "**3:00–4:00 — Honest result.** The model improves ranking, but unranked pages and uncertain cases are explicitly routed to human review. The model is not an automated content editor.\n",
        "\n",
        "**4:00–5:00 — Recommendation.** Keep the no-go rules, monitor the validation baseline monthly, and move to a genuine prior-window → future-window label before making stronger predictive claims.\n"
      ]
